            <abstract lang="en">
                <p>The present invention implements high-speed right shift computation and division in secure computation. According to the present invention, a public value multiplication part 11 calculates [a']=[2&lt;u>a] from a distributed value [a] of a value "a." A first conversion part 12 converts [a'] into additive secret sharing. A right shift computation part 13 calculates &lt;s>i=&lt;a'>i>>b+u. A second conversion part 14 converts &lt;s> into linear secret sharing. A first bit conversion part 15 converts lower u bits of &lt;a'>i into {a'i mod 2&lt;u>}. A quotient transfer part 16 obtains lower u bits of -Σi&lt;m {a'i mod 2&lt;u>} as {q}. A second bit conversion part 17 converts lower b+u bits of &lt;a'>i into {a'iR}={a'i mod 2&lt;b+u>}. An addition part 18 calculates {z}=Ei&lt;m{a'iR}+{q}, and obtains a bit sequence {zQ} of a (b+u)-th bit and after of {z}. A third conversion part 19 converts {q} and {zQ} into linear secret sharing. An output computation part 20 outputs [s]-[2&lt;1-(b+u)>q]+[zQ] as [a>>b].</p>
            </abstract>
